 config should this go? Let me think about the structure.\\n\\nLooking at the provided snippet:\\n```\\n\\\"models\\\": {\\n  \\\"mode\\\": \\\"merge\\\",\\n  \\\"providers\\\": {\\n    \\\"local\\\": {\\n      \\\"baseUrl\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"apiKey\\\": \\\"...\\\",\\n      \\\"api\\\": \\\"openai-completions\\\",\\n      \\\"models\\\": [\\n        { \\\"id\\\": \\\"MiniMax-M2.5\\\", ... }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis looks like it might be part of the `providers` section in the OpenClaw config. The structure suggests that within the config file, there's a `models` object that manages provider configurations with a merge mode.\\n\\nLet me read the actual config file first to understand the current structure and determine where exactly to add these models. I'll use exec with a read command.\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"text\",\n              \"text\": \"让我先查看当前的 OpenClaw 配置文件结构，然后按照这个格式添加 SCNet 的模型。\"\n            },\n            {\n              \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n              \"id\": \"call_784704d81a454d19a7bfac17\",\n              \"name\": \"sessions_spawn\",\n              \"arguments\": {\n                \"task\": \"1. Read the OpenClaw configuration file at ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json (or /etc/openclaw/config.yaml if that exists)\\n2. Identify the structure around \\\"models\\\" and \\\"providers\\\" sections\\n3. Show me the current content, especially the \\\"models\\\": { \\\"mode\\\": \\\"merge\\\", \\\"providers\\\": { ... } } section if it exists\\n4. Then I'll guide adding the three SCNet models in the proper format\",\n                \"runtime\": \"subagent\",\n                \"mode\": \"run\"\n              }\n            }\n          ],\n          \"api\": \"openai-completions\",\n          \"provider\": \"openrouter\",\n          \"model\": \"openrouter/free\",\n          \"usage\": {\n            \"input\": 30861,\n            \"output\": 1073,\n            \"totalTokens\": 31934,\n