{"type":"message","id":"192632cb","parentId":"b9eeeb33","timestamp":"2026-03-29T08:41:11.091Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking me to troubleshoot why the subagents are always failing. Let me analyze the session history to identify the issues.\n\nLooking at the errors I've seen:\n1. \"510 Model Request Error\" - When trying to use scnet/DeepSeek-V3.2\n2. \"400 status code (no body)\" - When using Google Gemini\n3. \"model not allowed: scnet/MiniMax-2.5\" - When specifying invalid model names\n\nThe main issues seem to be:\n1. SCNet provider models are not properly configured - when using scnet/DeepSeek-V3.2 in subagents, it fails with \"510 Model Request Error\"\n2. The model names might not be valid - \"MiniMax-2.5\" isn't valid, it should be \"MiniMax-2.5\" but that's also wrong\n3. The openrouter/auto model seems to work better\n\nLooking at the current runtime info:\n- default_model: zai/glm-5\n- model: scnet/MiniMax-2.5\n\nThe main issue seems to be that:\n1. When I spawn subagents with scnet models, they fail with 510 errors\n2. When I use openrouter/auto, it works but returns incomplete results sometimes\n\nLet me check what's happening with the subagent configuration and see if there are any obvious configuration issues.\n\nActually, looking at the errors more carefully:\n- scnet/DeepSeek-V3.2: 510 Model Request Error\n- scnet/MiniMax-2.5: model not allowed\n- google/gemini-2.5-flash: 400 status code\n\nThe subagents are failing because the models aren't working properly in the subagent environment, not because of configuration issues with the skills themselves.\n\nI should check what the actual error is and report to the user. Let me also check the OpenClaw configuration to see what models are available.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\n好的，让我查一下子代理出错的原因。从历史记录来看，主要有以下几个错误：\n\n1. **510 Model Request Error** - 使用 scnet/DeepSeek-V3.2 时出错\n2. **model not allowed** - 使用 scnet/MiniMax-2.5 时模型名称不对\n3. **400 status code** - 使用 Google Gemini 时出错\n\n让我检查一下当前的配置和可用的模型：\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2fcb9bdfa4e141208bdb4110","name":"sessions_spawn","arguments":{"task":"Check the OpenClaw configuration and diagnose why subagents are failing with these errors:\n1. \"510 Model Request Error\" when using scnet models\n2. \"model not allowed: scnet/MiniMax-2.5\"\n\nCheck:\n1. ~/.openclaw/openclaw.json - look for models and providers config\n2. Check what models are available in the config\n3. Identify if scnet provider is properly configured\n\nOutput the relevant configuration sections.","runtime":"subagent","mode":"run","model":"openrouter/auto"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"scnet","model":"MiniMax-M2.5","usage":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":0,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774773629076,"responseId":"chatcmpl-1ae0bda236e7f92bc110f5abfa6b1198"}}
