{"type":"message","id":"cbccdf76","parentId":"094b2109","timestamp":"2026-03-29T08:57:44.161Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The openrouter model also failed with a different error: \"402 This request requires more credits, or fewer max_tokens. You requested up to 4096 tokens, but can only afford 990.\"\n\nThis is a credits issue with openrouter. The user needs to add credits to their openrouter account.\n\nLooking at the error, there are multiple issues:\n1. scnet models in subagents fail with \"510 Model Request Error\" - credentials not passed\n2. openrouter/auto fails with \"402\" - not enough credits\n\nThis is frustrating. The user is having trouble with subagents. Let me explain this to them and ask if they can provide the document content directly, or if they can help resolve the credentials issue.\n\nActually, wait - earlier in this conversation, I successfully read a Feishu document using a subagent. Let me check that session. The subagent used google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite or something and succeeded in reading a document. \n\nLooking back at the history, I see:\n- Agent:lucus:subagent:2d9bc640-... successfully read a document and returned content about \"2025年Q2整体计划\"\n\nSo the issue is intermittent or related to specific models. Let me try using google models since that seemed to work before.\n\nActually, from the session details I can see:\n- The document \"2025年Q2整体计划\" was successfully read by a subagent earlier\n- The user is now asking to read \"BxImwCq5ni38yekUvLwjc3SQpzf\" which is the same document\n\nWait - earlier I read \"BxImwCq5ni38yekUvLwjc3SQpzf\" and got \"2025年Q2整体计划\"! So that document is the quarterly plan, not ECHO protocol. Maybe the user is confused or gave me the wrong link.\n\n\nI should clarify with the user which specific document they want me to access, since I've already retrieved the quarterly plan from that link.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n\